---
import Page from '../layouts/Page.astro';
import Section from '../components/Section.astro';
import { constants } from '../constants';

const { mailingListUrl } = constants.meta;
const {
    sean: { email: seanEmail, site: seanSite },
    steph: { email: stephEmail, site: stephSite },
} = constants.contacts;

const mailtoSteph = `mailto:${stephEmail}`;
---

<Page
    title="Collaborate"
    description="Details on how you can work with us."
    heading="Collaborate with us"
    currentArea="collaborate"
>
    <p>
        Here's an introductory passage for the collaboration page. All the
        detail of the ways you can collaborate with us comes below.
    </p>
    <Fragment slot={'sections'}>
        <Section heading="Talks and Workshops">
            <p>
                We have run workshops for video game writers and producers, and
                regularly give talks to both specialist and general audiences.
                Topics include (but are not limited to) gender representation,
                optionality and agency, ethics in games, and writing more
                realistic dialogue.
            </p>
            <p>
                Contact <a href={mailtoSteph}>Steph</a> or <a
                    href=`mailto:${seanEmail}`>Seán</a
                > to organise a talk for your company, university, or event. If you’d
                like to attend more of our events, <a href={mailingListUrl}
                    >sign up for our mailing list</a
                >.
            </p>
        </Section>
        <Section heading="Research Collaborations">
            <p>
                If you or your company are looking for partners in new research
                on video games, we’d be <a href={mailtoSteph}
                    >delighted to chat with you</a
                >. You can <a
                    href="https://theconversation.com/nearly-a-third-of-female-gamers-feel-guilty-about-their-hobby-new-study-263752"
                    >read about our recent study on women’s attitudes to gaming</a
                > for an example of work undertaken with a games company. You can
                also <a href="/tools/">explore our tools</a>.
            </p>
        </Section>
        <Section heading="Consulting">
            <p>
                If you are looking for input or advice concerning your next
                project, we’re <a href={mailtoSteph}>only an email away</a>.
            </p>
        </Section>
        <Section heading="About us" id="about">
            <p>
                Steph Rennick is a games researcher, philosopher, and lecturer
                in interactive media at <a href={stephSite}
                    >the University of Stirling</a
                >. Seán Roberts is a quantitative linguist, games researcher,
                and senior lecturer at <a href={seanSite}>Cardiff University</a
                >.
            </p>
            <p>
                Together, we co-created the <a href="/tools/#vgdc"
                    >Video Game Dialogue Corpus</a
                >, the first large-scale, openly accessible, consistently coded
                corpus of video game dialogue, which we used to conduct the <a
                    href="https://royalsocietypublishing.org/doi/full/10.1098/rsos.221095"
                    >largest ever study of gender bias</a
                > in character dialogue in games. We have developed <a
                    href="https://gamestudies.org/2103/articles/rennick_roberts"
                    >new methods</a
                > and <a href="/tools/">tools</a> for studying games, and <a
                    href="/findings/">our research</a
                > has appeared in mainstream and gaming media internationally.
            </p>
            <p>
                Our work aims to empower gamemakers to make informed choices
                about representation, agency, and dialogue in their game design.
            </p>
        </Section>
    </Fragment></Page
>
